MODIFICATIONS
-------------

As required by Apache License 2.0 section 4(b), the following files have been
changed from their upstream versions. All changes exist to make the ggml Metal
backend work on AMD GCN GPUs, which execute 64-wide wavefronts, where upstream
assumes 32-wide Apple simdgroups.

Under external/ggml/ (MIT, The ggml authors):

    src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal.metal
    src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m
    src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.cpp
    src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-ops.cpp

        - runtime SIMD-width probe; N_SIMDWIDTH injected at both
          MTLCompileOptions sites instead of being hardcoded to 32
        - GGML_METAL_DEVICE selects a GPU by name or index, so a headless
          compute card can be used instead of the display GPU
        - wave-width-generic lane -> block mapping in the mat-vec kernels
        - kernel_mul_mm_w64: a register-tiled GEMM for GPUs without
          simdgroup_matrix support
        - concurrent dispatch restricted to Apple-family GPUs
        - correctness fixes at 64-wide: GGML_OP_SUM reduction count, iq-quant
          mat-vec threadgroup bounds, GATED_DELTA_NET shape admission
        - runtime dials: GGML_METAL_MM_W64_DISABLE, GGML_METAL_MM_MIN,
          GGML_METAL_MM_ID_MIN, GGML_METAL_N_CB, GGML_METAL_CONCURRENCY_ENABLE

Under src/ (Apache 2.0, ShugoAI LLC):

    src/framework/modules/transformers/qwen_decoder.cpp
    src/models/yue2/nar_runtime.cpp

        - AUDIOCPP_DISABLE_FLASH_ATTN takes the explicit attention paths these
          files already carry. FLASH_ATTN_EXT is gated on simdgroup_matrix
          support and aborts rather than falling back, so without this the run
          dies on AMD.

